# GitHub does not automatically retry failed App webhooks.  This offline gate pins the bounded, metadata-only,
# durable recovery protocol without requiring network access or credentials.
register_gate "tests/test_failed_webhook_recovery.py" "FAILED WEBHOOK RECOVERY GATE: PASS" "failed GitHub webhook recovery protocol" "failed GitHub webhooks are recovered by Core with App-JWT metadata-only pagination, durable scan/retry authority, exact eligibility, bounded work, and active alerts" "GitHub App failed-delivery recovery: list metadata only (never detail/body); persist epoch/HWM/opaque cursor plus durable page-tail ordering and expected-cursor CAS; group GUID newest-state with any-success sticky; resolve exact OK plus GitHub's 200-399 success range or local receipts; retry every explicit bounded non-OK delivery including missing-code, 3xx, 4xx, 5xx, and exact Timed Out; precommit before one ACK-ambiguous POST; hard max-three attempts; durable 403/429 global pause; Unknown/inconsistent-OK outcomes fail closed with durable evidence; fleet singleflight; keep full unresolved rows for 30 days after the replay window then boundedly compact them to non-paging aggregate counters; scan-lag/terminal/exhausted alerts; no new secret or env knob" 20
